      "output": "## Container decision: executable script, not a skill\n\nThis job is fully deterministic — sort JSON keys lexicographically, error on duplicate keys. There is no ambiguous acceptance, no agent judgment, and no behavioral variation across contexts. The skill development guidance is explicit: \"Keep deterministic mechanics in scripts so agents execute them without loading their implementation.\" Wrapping this in a skill adds overhead without adding value; agents should invoke the script directly.\n\nThe right container is a standalone executable script (e.g., `scripts/sort_json.py`) that agents call as a tool or shell step.\n\n---\n\n## Completion check\n\nAll of the following must hold for a run to be accepted:\n\n1. **Exit code 0** — the script exits non-zero and prints the first offending key path on any duplicate key detection; a zero exit means no duplicates were found.\n2. **Valid JSON output** — the output parses as JSON without error.\n3. **Duplicate-free** — a second pass with a strict-mode JSON parser (or the script itself in verify mode) reports zero duplicate keys at every nesting level.\n4. **Deterministic key order** — keys at every object level are in lexicographic ascending order; running `jq --sort-keys` on the output and diffing against the output itself produces no diff.\n5. **Idempotent** — running the script a second time on its own output produces byte-identical output (confirms stable sort and no side effects).\n6. **Value preservation** — a round-trip value check (compare all leaf values between input and output, ignoring key order) reports zero missing or mutated values.",
